Subject: Bind ZeroClaw 0.8 agent tool roots to the benchmark fixture

Apply after 0001-medicalharness-runner-changes.patch.

Observed on installed ZeroClaw 0.8.5 (2026-09-09): content_search with no
path or path='.', plus shell pwd, use <config-dir>/agents/<alias>/workspace.
Neither subprocess cwd nor ZEROCLAW_WORKSPACE changes that per-agent root.
allowed_roots grants absolute-path access but does not choose the default.
Bind each configured agent's workspace.path to the task fixture, preserving
the existing TOML, provider rewrites, risk profiles, and legacy behavior.

Verified with five model-free regression tests and a localhost canned-provider
canary against the actual installed binary. No real model was called.
Prior Qwen ZeroClaw runs used the uncorrected environment; successful absolute
searches do not establish equivalence for relative-tool behavior. Corrected
runs must carry this environment revision; rerun Qwen for strict comparison.

--- a/src/harnessbench/adapters/zeroclaw.py
+++ b/src/harnessbench/adapters/zeroclaw.py
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 from __future__ import annotations

+import json
 import os
 import re
 import shutil
@@ -102,6 +103,43 @@
